<!--
  ============================================================================
  Armoury_LightsaberCraftingCut.xml         Jawa_Armoury · authored 2026-09-03
  ============================================================================
  LIGHTSABER_RECIPE_GATE_1

  Owner, 2026-09-03, on the research-tree v4 pass: "they won't be teaching
  how to make lightsabers. Nobody will. That's not tech in this scenario."
  v4 accordingly cut the ResearchProjectDefs
  guy762_ResearchKotOR_lightsabers/_advsabers/_saberparts/_jedi. Cutting the
  RESEARCH does not stop the CRAFTING: lee.theforce.lightsaber
  (workshop 3466124712) ships its own crafting recipes on an abstract parent,
  `Lightsaber_Crafting`, that eight concrete recipes inherit by ParentName —
  none of the eight override `recipeUsers`.

  ARMOURY_LIGHTSABER_FINDMOD_1 (2026-09-04): this mod's absorbed copy of the
  donor's Patch_KotORLightsaberRecipes.xml was DELETED, not fixed. RimWorld
  runs a mod's top-level Patches/*.xml before its subfolder patch files, so
  this file's Remove of the abstract's recipeUsers ran first and the absorbed
  Replace of that same node then matched nothing - one FindMod "failed" line
  every load (proven by deploy-side bisection on the 17-mod repro list, 33s
  cycles). The failure also aborted its whole PatchOperationSequence, so the
  absorbed per-recipe research/ingredient ops NEVER ran on any load. Every op
  in that file existed to wire up lightsaber crafting benches and research -
  the exact thing the ruling above cuts - so the file is contradiction, not
  compatibility. If the crafting cut is ever reversed, recover the donor ops
  from git or the still-subscribed donor (workshop 2938932438).

  WHAT THE RESOLVED DUMP ACTUALLY SHOWS - read from the RESOLVED state, not
  the raw donor file, per this item's own criteria
  ============================================================================
  guy762.KotORWeapons (absorbed into this mod, WEAPONS_DONOR_RETIREMENT_1)
  shipped its OWN compatibility patch for this exact donor
  (Absorbed_AdditionalMods/kotorweapons/TheForceLightsabers/..._Patch_
  KotORLightsaberRecipes.xml, gated IfModActive="lee.theforce.lightsaber",
  active on the live 589-mod list) that already overrides the abstract
  parent's `recipeUsers` to [FabricationBench, guy762_KotORWorkbench] and
  adds `researchPrerequisite=guy762_ResearchKotOR_lightsabers` to each of the
  eight children — NOT the raw donor's own
  MicroelectronicsBasics/ElectricSmithy/FueledSmithy/TableMachining. Verified
  against `defs/RecipeDef.json` in capture 2026-09-03T07-26-04Z (589 mods,
  fingerprint-matched): `Force_CraftLightsaberSingle` resolves with
  `researchPrerequisite: guy762_ResearchKotOR_lightsabers`,
  `recipeUsers: [FabricationBench, guy762_KotORWorkbench]`.

  So once the v4 cuts land, this recipe's OWN researchPrerequisite is a
  dangling reference to a research project that no longer exists — which
  resolves to null, not to "unresearched forever". A null
  researchPrerequisite reads as NO PREREQUISITE, so the hole this item found
  is not "still needs unrelated tech", it is "needs no research at all"
  once the cut research project is gone. Removing `recipeUsers` on the
  shared abstract parent closes it regardless of which research field ends
  up governing it — a recipe attached to zero benches cannot be queued from
  any bench, independent of research state, and this is the ONE field
  neither the raw donor's own file nor the absorbed compat patch's overrides
  touch per-child, so removing it here on the parent removes it for all
  eight inheritors in one place. Order relative to the absorbed compat
  patch's own PatchOperationReplace on this same xpath does not matter:
  whichever runs first, this Remove is the one that is still standing when
  inheritance resolves, because a PatchOperationReplace targeting a node
  this Remove has already deleted matches nothing and is a silent no-op
  (project doctrine: PatchOperationReplace/Conditional/FindMod all return
  true on no match), and if this Remove runs second it simply deletes
  whatever the Replace most recently wrote.

  ITEMS ARE UNTOUCHED - migration rule 5
  ============================================================================
  This removes ONLY `recipeUsers` from the shared RecipeDef parent. Every
  lightsaber ThingDef, its stats, its market value and its lootability are
  completely unaffected — a lightsaber still exists, still drops from a
  body, still trades. Only MAKING one, at any bench, goes away.

  SAFETY
  ======
  Gated on `lee.theforce.lightsaber` being active at all via
  PatchOperationFindMod (this patch is meaningless without that donor); NOT
  additionally wrapped in a PatchOperationConditional on the xpath existing,
  deliberately — if `Lightsaber_Crafting` or its `recipeUsers` node is ever
  renamed upstream, this should show up as a validate_patch.py xpath-miss,
  not vanish as a second silent no-op stacked on top of the first gate.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <li>Star Wars : The Force - Lightsaber</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationRemove">
      <xpath>Defs/RecipeDef[@Name="Lightsaber_Crafting"]/recipeUsers</xpath>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
